# Per-package coverage floors, enforced by scripts/coverage.sh in CI.
#
# Ratchet-only: raise a floor when a package earns it, never lower one to make
# a red build green. A package listed here that no longer exists is an error,
# not a skip. That is how a deleted or renamed package gets noticed.
#
# Targets from the plan, applied as each package lands:
#   internal/packwiz  95   it deletes files on player machines
#   internal/mcevents 95   pure parsing, no excuse for a gap
#   internal/bench    90   a silent misparse invalidates every number  [met: 98]

# Lowered from 70 deliberately, and the total raised from 75 to 80 in the same
# change. cmd/wly gained docker.go: a shell-out adapter with no decisions in it,
# added so that the run orchestration could move into internal/bench and be
# tested against a replayed log. The gate got stricter overall - the package
# holding the logic is at 98 - while the package holding the I/O got thinner and
# less coverable. That is the trade being recorded, not a red build made green.
# Raised from 30 when the guild reconciler landed. The REST layer is testable
# against httptest in a way the docker shell-out never was, so the package
# earned it: 54.1 measured the CI way, with docker off PATH. Kept well short of
# that number on purpose, because D2 adds more thin I/O and a floor you land
# exactly on is a failure waiting for the next commit.
weloveyou-mc/cmd/wly              45
weloveyou-mc/cmd/wlyup            70
weloveyou-mc/internal/bench       99
weloveyou-mc/internal/buildinfo   85

# The guild reconciler decides what happens to a live community's roles and
# channels, so it is held to the same 95 as the other pure packages. It sits at
# 98.6; the floor keeps margin deliberately, because landing on the number is a
# failure waiting for the next commit.
weloveyou-mc/internal/discord     95

# The log parser and the stats reader. The plan's own target was 95 and it is
# the right number: a misparse here either fails to verify a real player or
# verifies the wrong one, and the stats feed every leaderboard and playtime
# role. Sits at 100, and the parser is fuzzed as well as covered.
weloveyou-mc/internal/mcevents    95

# Across every package. Rises as the logic-heavy packages land; the plan's
# destination is 85.
total                             80
